      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The mansion was designed by McKim, Mead, and White in a Beaux‑Arts style.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Staatsburg%2C_New_York",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Inside the estate sits the 1792 home of Revolutionary War general Morgan Lewis and his wife Gertrude Livingston.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://parks.ny.gov/visit/historic-sites/staatsburgh-state-historic-site",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Staatsburg got its name from Samuel Staats, a Dutch surgeon who bought land from the Pawling estate in the 1690s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Staatsburg%2C_New_York",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Hudson River views from the park make it a favorite spot for hiking, cycling, and camping.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Staatsburg%2C_New_York",
